  "Question": "If the sum of the distances equals the distance between the two foci, what is the locus?",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "An ellipse",
    "B": "A hyperbola",
    "C": "The line segment between the two foci",
    "D": "The entire plane"
  },
  "Correct Answer": "C",
  "Accepted Answers": [],
  "Unordered Answers": false,
  "Solution": "When the sum equals the distance between the foci, the point can only lie on the line segment joining the two foci, so the locus cannot form an ellipse.",
